  "about": "Perishables (#396): groups of fresh ingredients with a 'keeps about N days once bought' hint, for Shop for this week's second trip and the plan's 'cook it earlier?' note. An ingredient matches by the END of its name (IngredientName.of, with a listed singular and plural read as one word, names.json pluralPairs), longest alias first, exactly like the density table: 'smoked salmon' (skip) beats 'salmon' by being longer. skip lists names that would otherwise end in an alias but are not fresh (dried, frozen, canned, cooked, smoked, cured); a skip also wins a tie. minDays and maxDays are the hint's range, the cautious end of the published fridge-storage ranges (docs/decisions.md names the source of each group); they are a hint, never a date the app claims to know. The same keys and days in every language's file. Only fresh food that goes off within days belongs here; anything not listed is not perishable as far as the app says, and is bought now. Aliases are lowercase, hyphens written as spaces, apostrophes left out.",
